-- title:
--   Labelled level automorphisms suffice for Igusa discs, q=2
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$ with $q=2$ and a nonzero $M'$ not divisible by $q$, together with a prime $\ell$ with $\ell\equiv 11\pmod{12}$ and $\ell\mid M'$; let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $q$ a non-unit of $A$, let $W$ be a finite set of places of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}$ of level $M'$ over the residue field of $A$, let $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'\le \mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ via `hle`, let $R_0$ be a constant reduction of $A$ on $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ with residual field $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}$, and let $\zeta$ be a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$. Let $OIg$ assign a valuation subring of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ to each point of $\mathbb P^1(\mathbb Z/q)$, with $OIg(\mathrm{lineInfty}\,q)$ characterised by `hIg_inf` as the set of $f$ admitting Laurent series $x,y$ over $A$ with $y$ having nonzero coefficientwise reduction and $f\cdot y=x$; let $R$ be a regular prolongation of $A$ on $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ with residual field $\mathrm{xHFunctionFieldC}$ of level $q^2M'$ and group $\mathrm{levelH}\,q\,M'$, whose ring of integers is $OIg(\mathrm{lineInfty}\,q)$. Let $NIg$ be a finite set of places of that residual field and $\mathrm{disc}$ a map sending each such place $Q$ to a set of places of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$. Assume, for every $\tau$ in the subgroup generated by the level automorphisms $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta'\,\gamma$ ($\zeta'$ any primitive $q$-th root of unity, $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$) which preserves $R$'s integers: the induced residual automorphism $R.\mathrm{resAut}\,\tau$ preserves $NIg$ (`hNstab`), and for $Q\notin NIg$ it carries $\mathrm{disc}(Q)$ to $\mathrm{disc}$ of the translated place (`hdiscstab`). Call a place $P$ of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ *untubed* when for each $s\in W$ it is false that: for every $f$ in the integers of $R_0$ whose order is nonnegative at every place where $\mathrm{jq}$ has nonnegative order, with $R_0$-residue lying in the valuation subring of $s$, and every $a\in A$ whose residue equals the value of that residue at $s$, the difference $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f)-a$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$. Assume `hδ`: every untubed $P$ satisfies $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma\cdot P\in\mathrm{disc}(Q)$ for some $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ and some $Q\notin NIg$. Finally let $g$ attach to each point $\lambda$ of $\mathbb P^1(\mathbb Z/q)$ an automorphism lying in the above subgroup and of the form $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma$ for some $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ with $\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma\cdot\mathrm{lineInfty}\,q=\lambda$. The conclusion: every untubed place $P$ admits a point $\lambda$ of $\mathbb P^1(\mathbb Z/q)$ and a place $Q\notin NIg$ with $g(\lambda)\cdot P\in\mathrm{disc}(Q)$.
--
--   This is a normalisation step in the assembly of a semistable covering of the full-level modular curve of level $q^2M'$ in the case $q=2$: it upgrades the existential statement that some level automorphism of $\Gamma_0(M')$ moves a place lying outside all the tubes attached to $W$ into a non-node Igusa disc, to the statement that one of the finitely many labelled automorphisms $g(\lambda)$, indexed by the points of $\mathbb P^1(\mathbb Z/q)$, already does so. It is used in the construction of the semistable covering and its equivalence clauses from valuation-subring data for the semistable model.
